+
+## Tipped bot vehicles: the original AI path (2026-10-14)
+
+**User report (package 4):** "a car tipped over and it was still moving forward even though the car was tipped forward".
+
+### What the original does
+
+From the decompiled scripts:
+- There is no forced transform, auto-reset or roll clamp.
+- **Bots** in hover form do not run the player simulation. TnCarForm / TnTankForm.Hovering.DoUpdateAi calls UpdateFromLocationAndRotation, which uses:
+  - HoverPhysics.MoveToTargetLocation: world-horizontal velocity toward the target at AiMaxLinearSpeed / AiMaxLinearAcceleration;
+  - HoverPhysics.RotateToTargetOrientation: toward DesiredRotation (the focus direction, Pitch 0, roll 0). Pitch and roll are only included once IsUnstable (car / truck: pitch or roll over 30 deg) or !IsStable (tank).
+- So a tipped AI hover vehicle is turned back to level, at AiMaxAngularSpeed / AiMaxAngularAcceleration (authored: car 12 / 12, truck 20 / 20, tank 6 / 6, in rad/s and rad/s^2), and keeps translating while it rights.
+- **Players:** UpdateTurn rights the body only with no spring contact or upside down (up.Z < 0.01).
+- **Driving:** DoUpdateAi is a no-op in the Driving state. AI cars in Driving run the player CarSimulation.
+
+### What the rebuild did
+
+- Bots ran the player hover path.
+- Pitch and roll are clamped to +-1.2 rad, so "upside down" is unreachable. A tipped body that kept one spring contact never righted, and its body-frame strafe kept pushing it.
+
+### What is ported
+
+| Part of the AI path | Status |
+|---|---|
+| RotateToTargetOrientation on pitch / roll while unstable | **Ported**, authored limits |
+| MoveToTargetLocation translation | **Ported only while unstable**: toward the bot's move direction, replacing the stand-in strafe |
+| Translation while stable | **Not ported**: bots keep the player-style strafe (the stand-in), so normal bot driving is unchanged |
+| AI yaw control | Not ported |
+| Driving state | Unchanged (the original has no AI path there either) |
+| Jets | Unaffected (jetStep) |
+
+This change affects both Smart and Classic (shared vehicle code). The Classic identity gate is re-based from integration 56290b7d + this patch.
+
+### Measurements
+
+**Tipped time** (null-render NAVQ, Smart; summed hover-vehicle episodes over 1 s, seeds 1-3; old -> (a) righting only -> (b) righting + translation):
+
